From 9994d6a27257c908266fbd3414743c75037c4e3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: devernay <devernay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:06:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add an OSMesa framework (PIGLIT_USE_OSMESA, platform osmesa)

Creates the GL context with OSMesaCreateContextAttribs (core or
compatibility profile, the version the test asks for) on an RGBA buffer
in memory, with no window system: no Waffle, GLUT, GLX or EGL. Swapping
buffers does nothing, and -fbo renders to an FBO as the Waffle FBO
framework does. piglit-dispatch looks up every GL function with
OSMesaGetProcAddress, which also works with a mangled OSMesa (mgl*).

CMake: -DPIGLIT_USE_OSMESA=ON -DOSMesa_LIBRARIES=<library and its
dependencies> -DOSMesa_INCLUDE_DIR=<dir with GL/osmesa.h>. Tests then
link OSMesa_LIBRARIES in place of the GL library. Python: platform
osmesa (piglit run -p osmesa).
